# Build artifacts (see CLAUDE.md: "build artifacts (*.o/*.mod/*.x) ... routinely
# show up as untracked/modified in git status and are not meaningful diffs on
# their own" -- tracking them was a pre-existing mistake this formalizes fixing).
*.o
*.mod
*.x

# Run outputs and scratch, TOP LEVEL ONLY.  The leading slash matters: the
# 3bodydata_*/ dataset directories hold tracked parameter files whose names also
# end in .dat, so a bare *.dat would be wrong.
/*.dat
/*.log
/*.scratch
/fort.*

# Bulk tabulated arrays inside dataset directories -- multi-MB numerical output,
# regenerable by Adiabatic-Scattering-BoundStates from the .par.used recipe kept
# alongside them.  The small PARAMETER/metadata files in the same directories
# (Fit.data, FitLeff.data, masses.dat, *.par.used) ARE tracked, so a clone can see
# what any dataset contains -- channel count, thresholds, Leff, fit window, masses
# -- without carrying the arrays themselves.
#
# Note: datasets committed before this rule keep their arrays tracked (gitignore
# does not affect already-tracked files).  That asymmetry is deliberate: the rule
# applies going forward rather than rewriting history.
3bodydata_*/Uad.dat
3bodydata_*/Pmat.dat
3bodydata_*/Qmat.dat
3bodydata_*/dPmat.dat
3bodydata_*/VQmat.dat
3bodydata_*/Quick*.dat

# macOS
.DS_Store
